# Nursing Patient Flow

Ward nursing owns inpatient vitals, MAR, nursing notes, care tasks, handover, and discharge nursing clearance; keep all work attached to the IPD admission and keep ICU stay mutations outside this flow.

## Stage Sequence

- Receive handover from OPD, emergency, admission desk, theater, or ICU.
- Complete the ward admission checklist.
- Run the ward care loop: vitals, observations, nursing notes, MAR, and care tasks.
- Support doctor review and transfer preparation.
- Receive post-op or ICU step-down handoff when applicable.
- Complete nursing clearance before final IPD discharge.

## Handoffs

- Ward nurse owns the admission checklist and ongoing bedside care.
- Charge nurse owns transfer support and escalation coordination.
- Doctor owns clinical orders and discharge decisions.
- ICU owns critical-care stay start and end.
- Pharmacy owns dispensing; nursing only records administration.

## Hard Invariants

- Must not create or manage IPD admission records.
- Must not start or end ICU stays from ward workflows.
- Must not duplicate pharmacy dispensing or discharge finalization.
- Must keep OPD vitals on the OPD encounter only.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Show shared vitals and MAR visibility for ward context.
- Surface pending meds, handover items, and alert trends for review.
- Use the IPD encounter id for all ward panels and mutations.
- Route ICU escalation to ICU flow instead of local ICU CRUD.

